				\begin{document}$${\beta }_{2}=0.9$$\end{document}β2=0.999, weight decay of 0.1 and dropout of 0.0. The batch size is nine and the gradients are accumulated during ten batches before running the backward pass. The minimum learning rate is 1 × 10−5, which increases until 1 × 10−3 with a linear warmup of 100,000 steps. After the warmup, a cosine decay regime82 is applied. Gradient clipping is set to 1.0 during the first epoch and then decreased to 0.5. All weights are initialized using Xavier initialization83 with default parameters, while the bias terms are initialized to 0. Checkpoints were taken every 10,000 steps.

